  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A school wants to plan a trip for a group of KKK students and **one** mentor.\n\nA hotel is booked for their stay, where the rooms are formatted in form of a matrix AAA with NNN rows and MMM columns. There are a total of N×MN\\times MN×M rooms where the room (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) has a capacity of A(i,j)A_{(i,j)}A(i,j)​ people.\n\nThe distance between the rooms (i1,j1)(i_1, j_1)(i1​,j1​) and (i2,j2)(i_2, j_2)(i2​,j2​) is given by max⁡(∣i1−i2∣,∣j1−j2∣)\\max( |i_1-i_2| , |j_1-j_2| )max(∣i1​−i2​∣,∣j1​−j2​∣), where ∣X∣|X|∣X∣ denotes the absolute value of XXX.\n\nTo ensure that the trip goes smoothly, the rooms should be booked in a way such that the distance between the mentor's room and the farthest room of a student is **minimal**.\n\nNote that the mentor and students can stay in the **same** room.\n\nYour task is to find the **minimal distance** between the mentor's room and the farthest room of a student.\n\nIn case the total capacity of the hotel is less than K+1K+1K+1, print −1-1−1 instead.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains three space-separated integers N,M,N, M,N,M, and KKK — the number of rows, columns, and students, respectively.\nThe next NNN lines contain MMM space-separated integers each, denoting the capacity of each room.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the **minimal** distance between the mentor's room and the farthest room of a student.\n\n\nIn case the total capacity of the hotel is less than K+1K+1K+1, print −1-1−1 instead.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤5001 \\leq T \\leq 5001≤T≤500",
      "1≤N,M≤1061 \\leq N, M \\leq 10^{6}1≤N,M≤106",
      "1≤K≤1091 \\leq K \\leq 10^{9}1≤K≤109",
      "0≤A(i,j)≤1050 \\leq A_{(i,j)} \\leq 10^{5}0≤A(i,j)​≤105",
      "The sum of N⋅MN\\cdot MN⋅M over all test cases won't exceed 10610^{6}106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
