        "output": "3\n0\n-1\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Mentor can stay in room (1,2)(1, 2)(1,2), two students in room (1,1)(1, 1)(1,1), one student in room (1,4)(1, 4)(1,4) and two students in room (1,5)(1, 5)(1,5).\nThe farthest room of a student would be (1,5)(1, 5)(1,5) with distance 333.\nWe can show that in no other arrangement, we can achieve a distance less than 333.\nTest case 222: Mentor and all 333 students can stay in room (1,3)(1, 3)(1,3). Thus, the distance is 000.\nTest case 333: The hotel does not have enough capacity."
